# أوامر Codex لبناء نظام إدارة برنامج UTC

## الأمر 1: إنشاء المشروع

```text
Create a full-stack Arabic RTL SaaS web application for managing the UTC children's strengths assessment program.

Use:
- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Prisma ORM
- PostgreSQL
- NextAuth or Auth.js for authentication
- Role-based access control
- Multi-tenant architecture

The system must support multiple organizations. Each organization has its own users and data. Super Admin can see all organizations. Organization users can only see their own organization data.

The UI must be fully Arabic RTL.

Brand colors:
- Berry: #D6085C
- Ocean: #007AA9
- Sun: #F8D942
- Cloud: #EFEFE8
- Black: #1D1D1B
```

## الأمر 2: إنشاء الأدوار والصلاحيات

```text
Implement role-based access control with the following roles:

1. SUPER_ADMIN
- Can manage all organizations
- Can manage all users
- Can view all dashboards
- Can view and export all reports
- Can override workflow restrictions

2. ORG_ADMIN
- Can manage only their organization
- Can add children
- Can manage supervisors
- Can enter assessment results
- Can manage groups
- Can view organization reports

3. SUPERVISOR
- Can view assigned children
- Can confirm story completion
- Can add child notes
- Can confirm exercise completion
- Can upload attachments

4. TRAINER
- Can manage training sessions
- Can confirm attendance
- Can manage exercise schedules

Every API route must validate:
- logged-in user
- role permissions
- organization ownership
```

## الأمر 3: Prisma schema

```text
Create a Prisma schema with the following models:

Organization:
id, name, type, city, contactName, contactPhone, contactEmail, childrenTargetCount, startDate, expectedEndDate, status, createdAt, updatedAt

User:
id, organizationId nullable, name, email, phone, passwordHash, role, status, createdAt, updatedAt

Child:
id, organizationId, name, internalCode, age, gender, grade, motherName, motherPhone, supervisorId nullable, programStatus, createdAt, updatedAt

Story:
id, storyNumber, title, description, createdAt, updatedAt

ChildStory:
id, childId, storyId, status, completedAt nullable, confirmedBy nullable, notes nullable, createdAt, updatedAt

Strength:
id, name, description, color, sortOrder, isActive, createdAt, updatedAt

Assessment:
id, childId, status, enteredBy nullable, enteredAt nullable, strength1Id nullable, strength2Id nullable, strength3Id nullable, reportUrl nullable, notes nullable, createdAt, updatedAt

Group:
id, organizationId, name, strengthId, supervisorId nullable, trainerId nullable, status, createdAt, updatedAt

GroupChild:
id, groupId, childId, createdAt

TrainingSession:
id, organizationId, title, date, time, trainerId nullable, targetAudience, status, createdAt, updatedAt

TrainingAttendance:
id, sessionId, attendeeName, attendeeType, phone, childId nullable, status, confirmedAt nullable, notes nullable, createdAt, updatedAt

Exercise:
id, strengthId, title, description, duration, toolsRequired, instructions, successIndicators, createdAt, updatedAt

ExerciseSchedule:
id, groupId, exerciseId, date, time, assignedTo nullable, status, completedAt nullable, notes nullable, createdAt, updatedAt

Attachment:
id, organizationId, relatedType, relatedId, fileUrl, fileType, uploadedBy, createdAt

ActivityLog:
id, userId, organizationId nullable, action, entityType, entityId, createdAt

Notification:
id, organizationId nullable, title, message, type, status, createdAt, readAt nullable

Use enums where appropriate for role, status, programStatus, storyStatus, assessmentStatus, groupStatus, sessionStatus, attendanceStatus, exerciseScheduleStatus.
```

